/-!
# Reduction of the local Lefschetz situation to the complete case

Let `(A, f)` be a local Lefschetz situation and let `Â` be the `𝔪`-adic completion of `A`. Then
`(Â, f)` is again a local Lefschetz situation, and `Â` is `f`-adically complete. This file builds
that situation and identifies the punctured spectra of `Â` and of `Â / fÂ` with the base changes
to `Spec Â` of the punctured spectra of `A` and of `A / fA` that Stacks 0BLI and Stacks 0BLL
speak of. Combining the two it reduces both conclusions of the chapter — full faithfulness of
`FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` and the existence of a finite étale extension of a cover of `U` over `X` — to
the case of an `f`-adically complete base.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.LocalLefschetzSituation.completion` — the local Lefschetz situation of the
  `𝔪`-adic completion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.LocalLefschetzSituation.Annihilated` — the hypothesis of Stacks 0BM6 that
  `H¹_𝔪(A)` and `H²_𝔪(A)` are annihilated by a power of `f`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.LocalLefschetzSituation.DepthDim` — the hypotheses (a) and (c)(ii) of
  Stacks 0EK5: a dualizing complex, and `depth(A_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭) > 2` for `f ∉ 𝔭`.

## Main results

* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.isAdicComplete_completion` — the completed situation is `f`-adically
  complete, by Stacks 090T.
* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.annihilated_completion` — the annihilation hypothesis passes to the
  completion, by Stacks 0ALZ.
* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.depthDim_completion` — the dualizing-complex and depth-plus-dimension
  hypotheses pass to the completion, by Stacks 0BFR and Stacks 0EHW.
* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_isAdicCompleteCase` — the
  reduction of full faithfulness to the `f`-adically complete case, through Stacks 0BLI.
* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.exists_finiteEtale_extension_of_isAdicCompleteCase` — the reduction
  of the existence of a finite étale extension to the `f`-adically complete case, through
  Stacks 0BLL.

Both reductions take the side conditions of the result being reduced as an abstract predicate
`P` on local Lefschetz situations together with the hypothesis that `P` passes from `A` to `Â`,
and that hypothesis is supplied here for the two predicates the chapter needs.
`annihilated_completion` is Stacks 0ALZ: local cohomology commutes with the flat base change
`A → Â` and the maximal ideal of `Â` is `𝔪Â`, so `H^i_{𝔪Â}(Â) = Â ⊗_A H^i_𝔪(A)` is killed by the
image of the same power of `f`. `depthDim_completion` is Stacks 0BFR for the dualizing complex of
the complete local ring `Â` together with the second display of Stacks 0EHW, which says that
`depth + dim` is unchanged by the completion.

## Implementation notes

The two tags being applied are stated in terms of categorical pullbacks: Stacks 0BLI assumes
full faithfulness of restriction from `U ×_X Spec Â` to its own closed fibre, and the right-hand
side of Stacks 0BLL speaks of covers of `U ×_X Spec Â`. What is proved here is that the punctured
spectrum of `Â` *is* such a pullback — the preimage of `U` under `Spec Â ⟶ Spec A` is the
punctured spectrum of `Â`, because the maximal ideal of `Â` is generated by that of `A` — and
that the punctured spectrum of `Â / fÂ` is the corresponding pullback of `U₀`, which on rings is
the identification `(A / fA) ⊗_A Â = Â / fÂ`. Transporting full faithfulness along the resulting
isomorphism of arrows uses that base change of finite étale covers along an isomorphism is an
equivalence of categories.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 090T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ALZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ALZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BFR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BFR)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing
open Stacks.FundamentalGroup
open Stacks.LocalCohomology (localCohomologyDerived localCohomologyModule
  localCohomologyModuleFlatBaseChangeIso)
open Stacks.Algebraization (enatToEInt krullDimToEInt)
open scoped TensorProduct
open scoped ChangeOfRings

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace LocalLefschetzSituation

/-- The local Lefschetz situation of the `𝔪`-adic completion: the completion `Â` of a Noetherian
local ring is again Noetherian local, and the image of `f` lies in its maximal ideal because that
maximal ideal is generated by the one of `A`. -/
public def completion (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u} where
  A := AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A
  f := algebraMap S.A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) S.f
  f_mem_maximalIdeal := by
    rw [AdicCompletion.maximalIdeal_eq_map]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ S.f_mem_maximalIdeal

/-- A Noetherian local ring that is `𝔪`-adically complete is `g`-adically complete for every
`g ∈ 𝔪`: the ideal `(g)` is contained in `𝔪` and is finitely generated, so this is Stacks 090T. -/
private lemma isAdicComplete_span_of_mem_maximalIdeal (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B]
    [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal B) B] {g : B} (hg : g ∈ maximalIdeal B) :
    IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {g}) B :=
  isAdicComplete_of_le_of_fg_of_isAdicComplete
    (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hg)) inferInstance
    (Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_singleton g))

/-- The completed situation is `f`-adically complete. -/
public lemma isAdicComplete_completion (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) :
    IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {S.completion.f}) S.completion.A :=
  isAdicComplete_span_of_mem_maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A)
    S.completion.f_mem_maximalIdeal

/-- If `a` annihilates every element of the `A`-module `M`, then on a pure tensor of the base
change of `M` along `φ : A →+* B` the scalar `φ a` moves across: `(φ a · s) ⊗ m = s ⊗ a • m`,
which is `s ⊗ 0`. -/
private lemma tmul_smul_eq_zero {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B)
    {M : ModuleCat.{u} A} (a : A) (h : ∀ m : M, a • m = 0) (s : B) (m : M) :
    (φ a * s) ⊗ₜ[A,φ] (m : M) = 0 := by
  let _ := φ.toAlgebra
  rw [show (φ a * s) ⊗ₜ[A,φ] (m : M) = s ⊗ₜ[A,φ] (a • m) from TensorProduct.smul_tmul a s m,
    h m, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]

/-- If `a` annihilates every element of the `A`-module `M`, then `φ a` annihilates every element
of the base change of `M` along `φ : A →+* B`: multiplication by `φ a` is a `B`-linear
endomorphism of the base change which vanishes on the pure tensors `1 ⊗ m`, hence vanishes. -/
private lemma smul_eq_zero_extendScalars {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    (φ : A →+* B) {M : ModuleCat.{u} A} (a : A) (h : ∀ m : M, a • m = 0)
    (z : (ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj M) : φ a • z = 0 := by
  have hzero : ModuleCat.ofHom
      (LinearMap.lsmul B ((ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj M) (φ a)) =
      (0 : (ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj M ⟶ (ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj M) :=
    ModuleCat.ExtendScalars.hom_ext_one_tmul φ fun m => tmul_smul_eq_zero φ a h 1 m
  change ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.lsmul B ((ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj M) (φ a)) z = 0
  rw [hzero]
  rfl

/-- **Annihilation of local cohomology by a power of an element passes to a flat base change.**
Let `φ : A →+* B` be flat, let `I ⊆ A` be finitely generated and let `J = IB`. If `g ^ n`
annihilates `H^i_{V(I)}(A)`, then `φ g ^ n` annihilates `H^i_{V(J)}(B)`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0ALZ] read on the cohomology modules, which is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyModuleFlatBaseChangeIso`: it identifies `H^i_{V(J)}(B)`
with `B ⊗_A H^i_{V(I)}(A)` — the base ring is carried to the base ring by
`ModuleCat.ExtendScalars.objSelfIso` — and in a base change the scalar `φ g ^ n` moves onto the
second factor, where it already acts by zero. -/
private theorem exists_pow_smul_localCohomologyModule_map_eq_zero {A B : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B) (hφ : φ.Flat) (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG) {J : Ideal B} (hJ : J.FG)
    (hIJ : I.map φ = J) (g : A) (i : ℤ)
    (h : ∃ n, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule A I hI (ModuleCat.of A A) i, g ^ n • x = 0) :
    ∃ n, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule B J hJ (ModuleCat.of B B) i, φ g ^ n • x = 0 := by
  subst hIJ
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := h
  refine ⟨n, fun x => ?_⟩
  let e : localCohomologyModule B (I.map φ) hJ (ModuleCat.of B B) i ≅
      (ModuleCat.extendScalars φ).obj (localCohomologyModule A I hI (ModuleCat.of A A) i) :=
    (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} B) i).mapIso
        ((localCohomologyDerived B (I.map φ) hJ).mapIso
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} B) 0).mapIso
            (ModuleCat.ExtendScalars.objSelfIso φ).symm)) ≪≫
      localCohomologyModuleFlatBaseChangeIso φ hφ I hI (ModuleCat.of A A) i
  refine e.toLinearEquiv.injective ?_
  rw [map_smul, map_zero, ← map_pow]
  exact smul_eq_zero_extendScalars φ (g ^ n) hn _

/-- **The annihilation hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0BM6]:** both `H¹_𝔪(A)` and `H²_𝔪(A)` are
annihilated by a power of `f`. This is the predicate on local Lefschetz situations that the
carriers of Stacks 0BM6 and Stacks 0BLS assume, in the spelling they assume it. -/
public def Annihilated (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) : Prop :=
  (∃ n, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule S.A (maximalIdeal S.A)
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal S.A)) (ModuleCat.of S.A S.A) 1,
      S.f ^ n • x = 0) ∧
    ∃ n, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule S.A (maximalIdeal S.A)
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal S.A)) (ModuleCat.of S.A S.A) 2,
      S.f ^ n • x = 0

/-- **The annihilation hypothesis passes to the `𝔪`-adic completion.** If `H¹_𝔪(A)` and `H²_𝔪(A)`
are annihilated by a power of `f`, then so are `H¹_{𝔪Â}(Â)` and `H²_{𝔪Â}(Â)`, with the same
exponents.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0ALZ] applied to the local Lefschetz situation: `A → Â` is flat because `A`
is Noetherian, the maximal ideal of `Â` is `𝔪Â`, and local cohomology therefore commutes with
that base change, so `H^i_{𝔪Â}(Â) = Â ⊗_A H^i_𝔪(A)` is annihilated by the image of the same power
of `f`. It is the hypothesis `hPcompletion` of the two reductions below, for the predicate
`Annihilated`. -/
public lemma annihilated_completion (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) (h : S.Annihilated) :
    S.completion.Annihilated := by
  have hflat : (algebraMap S.A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A)).Flat :=
    RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff.mpr inferInstance
  have hmap : (maximalIdeal S.A).map
      (algebraMap S.A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A)) =
      maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) :=
    AdicCompletion.maximalIdeal_eq_map.symm
  exact ⟨exists_pow_smul_localCohomologyModule_map_eq_zero _ hflat (maximalIdeal S.A)
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _) (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _) hmap S.f 1 h.1,
    exists_pow_smul_localCohomologyModule_map_eq_zero _ hflat (maximalIdeal S.A)
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _) (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _) hmap S.f 2 h.2⟩

/-- **The depth-plus-dimension inequality passes to the `𝔪`-adic completion**, stated for a
Noetherian local ring with a dualizing complex and an element `g`.

This is the second display of [Stacks, Tag 0EHW], which is
`Module.depth_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_adicCompletion`: for a prime `𝔭'` of `Â` lying over `𝔭`
in `A`, `depth(Â_{𝔭'}) + dim(Â/𝔭')` equals `depth(A_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭)`. A prime `𝔭'` avoiding the
image of `g` lies over a prime avoiding `g`, so the hypothesis applies there, and the two
spellings of the sum — in `WithBot ℕ∞` and in the extended integers — are matched by
a computation in the extended integers. -/
private lemma two_lt_depth_add_ringKrullDim_adicCompletion (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (hdual : ∃ K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A), Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex K) (g : A)
    (h : ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum A, g ∉ p.asIdeal →
      enatToEInt (Module.depth (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal)
          (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal))
          (LocalizedModule p.asIdeal.primeCompl A)) +
        krullDimToEInt (ringKrullDim (A ⧸ p.asIdeal)) > ((2 : ℤ) : EInt))
    (p : PrimeSpectrum (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A))
    (hp : algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A) g ∉ p.asIdeal) :
    enatToEInt (Module.depth (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal)
        (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal))
        (LocalizedModule p.asIdeal.primeCompl (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A))) +
      krullDimToEInt (ringKrullDim (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A ⧸ p.asIdeal)) >
      ((2 : ℤ) : EInt) := by
  have hbridge := congrArg krullDimToEInt
    (Module.depth_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_adicCompletion.{u, u, u} A hdual (maximalIdeal A)
      le_rfl A (p.asIdeal.under A) p.asIdeal)
  -- A depth and a dimension added in `WithBot ℕ∞` and then mapped to the extended integers give
  -- the sum of their images.
  have hcoe (x : ℕ∞) : krullDimToEInt (x : WithBot ℕ∞) = enatToEInt x := by
    cases x <;> rfl
  have hadd (x y : ℕ∞) : enatToEInt (x + y) = enatToEInt x + enatToEInt y := by
    cases x with
    | top =>
      cases y with
      | top => rfl
      | coe n =>
        change (⊤ : EInt) = ((⊤ : WithTop ℤ) : WithBot (WithTop ℤ)) +
          (((n : ℤ) : WithTop ℤ) : WithBot (WithTop ℤ))
        rw [← WithBot.coe_add, WithTop.top_add]
        rfl
    | coe m =>
      cases y with
      | top =>
        change (⊤ : EInt) = (((m : ℤ) : WithTop ℤ) : WithBot (WithTop ℤ)) +
          ((⊤ : WithTop ℤ) : WithBot (WithTop ℤ))
        rw [← WithBot.coe_add, WithTop.add_top]
        rfl
      | coe n =>
        change enatToEInt ((m : ℕ∞) + (n : ℕ∞)) =
          (((m : ℤ) : WithTop ℤ) : WithBot (WithTop ℤ)) +
            (((n : ℤ) : WithTop ℤ) : WithBot (WithTop ℤ))
        rw [← WithBot.coe_add, ← WithTop.coe_add, ← Nat.cast_add]
        change ((((m + n : ℕ) : ℤ) : WithTop ℤ) : WithBot (WithTop ℤ)) = _
        norm_cast
  have hcoe_add (x : ℕ∞) (y : WithBot ℕ∞) :
      krullDimToEInt ((x : WithBot ℕ∞) + y) = enatToEInt x + krullDimToEInt y := by
    cases y with
    | bot => cases x <;> rfl
    | coe z => rw [← WithBot.coe_add, hcoe, hcoe, hadd]
  rw [hcoe_add, hcoe_add] at hbridge
  exact lt_of_lt_of_eq (h ⟨p.asIdeal.under A, inferInstance⟩ hp) hbridge.symm

/-- **The hypotheses (a) and (c)(ii) of [Stacks, Tag 0EK5]:** `A` has a dualizing complex, and
`depth(A_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭) > 2` for every prime `𝔭 ⊂ A` with `f ∉ 𝔭`. This is the predicate on local
Lefschetz situations that the carriers of Stacks 0EK5 and Stacks 0EK6 assume, in the spelling
they assume it. -/
public def DepthDim (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) : Prop :=
  (∃ K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} S.A), Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex K) ∧
    ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum S.A, S.f ∉ p.asIdeal →
      enatToEInt (Module.depth (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal)
          (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal))
          (LocalizedModule p.asIdeal.primeCompl S.A)) +
        krullDimToEInt (ringKrullDim (S.A ⧸ p.asIdeal)) > ((2 : ℤ) : EInt)

/-- **The hypotheses (a) and (c)(ii) of Stacks 0EK5 pass to the `𝔪`-adic completion.** The
completion of a Noetherian local ring is Noetherian local and `𝔪Â`-adically complete, so it has
a dualizing complex by Stacks 0BFR, and the depth-plus-dimension inequality is carried over by
the second display of [Stacks, Tag 0EHW]. This is the hypothesis `hPcompletion` of the two
reductions below, for the predicate `DepthDim`. -/
public lemma depthDim_completion (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) (h : S.DepthDim) :
    S.completion.DepthDim :=
  ⟨Dualizing.exists_isDualizingComplex_of_isAdicComplete
      (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A),
    fun p hp => two_lt_depth_add_ringKrullDim_adicCompletion S.A h.1 S.f h.2 p hp⟩

/-- `Spec Â ⟶ Spec A`, the morphism of the `𝔪`-adic completion. -/
public def completionMap (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) : S.completion.X ⟶ S.X :=
  Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap S.A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A)))

/-- The preimage of the punctured spectrum of a Noetherian local ring `A` under
`Spec Â ⟶ Spec A` is the punctured spectrum of `Â`: a prime of `Â` contracts to the maximal ideal
of `A` exactly when it contains `𝔪Â`, and `𝔪Â` is the maximal ideal of `Â`. -/
private lemma preimage_puncturedSpectrum_specMap_algebraMap (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A] :
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A))) ⁻¹ᵁ
        Stacks.puncturedSpectrum A =
      Stacks.puncturedSpectrum (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A) := by
  ext x
  change PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A)) x ≠
      closedPoint A ↔ x ≠ closedPoint (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A)
  rw [← IsLocalRing.comap_closedPoint (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A))]
  refine not_congr ⟨fun h => ?_, fun h => by rw [h]⟩
  have h' : Ideal.comap (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A)) x.asIdeal =
      maximalIdeal A := by
    have h'' := congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal h
    rwa [IsLocalRing.comap_closedPoint] at h''
  have hle : maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A) ≤ x.asIdeal := by
    rw [AdicCompletion.maximalIdeal_eq_map, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    exact h'.ge
  exact PrimeSpectrum.ext
    (((maximalIdeal.isMaximal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A)).eq_of_le x.2.ne_top hle).symm)

/-- An open whose formation as a preimage is known sits in a cartesian square: the restriction of
`g` to the preimage of `V` exhibits that preimage as the base change of `V`. -/
private lemma exists_isPullback_of_preimage_eq {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : X ⟶ Y) (V : Y.Opens)
    {W : X.Opens} (hW : g ⁻¹ᵁ V = W) :
    ∃ r : W.toScheme ⟶ V.toScheme, IsPullback r W.ι V.ι g := by
  subst hW
  exact ⟨g ∣_ V, isPullback_morphismRestrict g V⟩

/-- The punctured spectrum of `Â` is the base change to `Spec Â` of the punctured spectrum
`U` of `A`. -/
public lemma exists_isPullback_completion_UOpen (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) :
    ∃ r : S.completion.U ⟶ S.U, IsPullback r S.completion.UOpen.ι S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap :=
  exists_isPullback_of_preimage_eq _ _ (preimage_puncturedSpectrum_specMap_algebraMap S.A)

/-- Taking a quotient commutes with a base change of rings: if the ideal `J ⊆ B` is generated by
the image of `I ⊆ A`, then `Spec (B / J)` is the base change of `Spec (A / I)` along
`Spec B ⟶ Spec A`. On rings this is the identification `(A / I) ⊗_A B = B / IB`. -/
private lemma exists_isPullback_specMap_quotient (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra A B] (I : Ideal A) {J : Ideal B} (hJ : I.map (algebraMap A B) = J) :
    ∃ c : Spec (.of (B ⧸ J)) ⟶ Spec (.of (A ⧸ I)),
      IsPullback c (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)))
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) := by
  subst hJ
  let e : CommRingCat.of ((A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] B) ≅ CommRingCat.of (B ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A B)) :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor B I).symm.toRingEquiv.toCommRingCatIso
  refine ⟨Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom ≫ e.hom),
    isPullback_SpecMap_of_isPushout _ _ _ _ ?_⟩
  refine (CommRingCat.isPushout_tensorProduct A (A ⧸ I) B).of_iso (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _)
    (Iso.refl _) e (by simp) (by simp) (by simp) ?_
  ext b
  exact ((Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor B I).symm_apply_eq).mpr
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor_mk B I b).symm

/-- `Spec (Â / fÂ)` is the base change to `Spec Â` of `X₀ = Spec (A / fA)`. -/
public lemma exists_isPullback_completion_X₀ (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) :
    ∃ c : S.completion.X₀ ⟶ S.X₀, IsPullback c S.completion.X₀ToX S.X₀ToX S.completionMap :=
  exists_isPullback_specMap_quotient S.A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) S.principalIdeal
    (J := Ideal.span {algebraMap S.A (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) S.f})
    (by rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton])

/-- The punctured spectrum `U₀'` of `Â / fÂ` is at once the base change of `U₀` along
`U' ⟶ U` and the base change of `U₀` along `X₀' ⟶ X₀`: pasting the cartesian square of the
completed situation with the two squares of the completion and cancelling the cartesian square
of `S` on the right. -/
public lemma exists_isPullback_completion_U₀ (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}) :
    ∃ (cU : S.completion.U ⟶ S.U) (c₀ : S.completion.X₀ ⟶ S.X₀) (u₀ : S.completion.U₀ ⟶ S.U₀),
      IsPullback cU S.completion.UOpen.ι S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap ∧
        IsPullback u₀ S.completion.U₀ToU S.U₀ToU cU ∧
          IsPullback u₀ S.completion.U₀Open.ι S.U₀Open.ι c₀ := by
  obtain ⟨cU, hcU⟩ := S.exists_isPullback_completion_UOpen
  obtain ⟨c₀, hc₀⟩ := S.exists_isPullback_completion_X₀
  have hcomm : (S.completion.U₀ToU ≫ cU) ≫ S.UOpen.ι
      = (S.completion.U₀Open.ι ≫ c₀) ≫ S.X₀ToX := by
    rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hcU.w, hc₀.w, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc,
      S.completion.isPullback_U₀ToU.w]
  refine ⟨cU, c₀, S.isPullback_U₀ToU.lift (S.completion.U₀ToU ≫ cU)
    (S.completion.U₀Open.ι ≫ c₀) hcomm, hcU, ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine IsPullback.of_right (h₁₂ := S.U₀Open.ι) ?_ (S.isPullback_U₀ToU.lift_fst ..)
      S.isPullback_U₀ToU.flip
    rw [S.isPullback_U₀ToU.lift_snd, hcU.w]
    exact S.completion.isPullback_U₀ToU.flip.paste_horiz hc₀
  · refine IsPullback.of_right (h₁₂ := S.U₀ToU) ?_ (S.isPullback_U₀ToU.lift_snd ..)
      S.isPullback_U₀ToU
    rw [S.isPullback_U₀ToU.lift_fst, hc₀.w]
    exact S.completion.isPullback_U₀ToU.paste_horiz hcU

/-- Post-composition with an isomorphism is an equivalence on finite étale covers: the two
composites are post-composition with an identity. -/
private def finiteEtaleOverMapEquivalence {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (e : X ≅ Y) :
    FiniteEtaleOver X ≌ FiniteEtaleOver Y :=
  .mk (MorphismProperty.Over.map ⊤ (MorphismProperty.of_isIso finiteEtale e.hom))
    (MorphismProperty.Over.map ⊤ (MorphismProperty.of_isIso finiteEtale e.inv))
    ((MorphismProperty.Over.mapId (P := finiteEtale) ⊤ X (e.hom ≫ e.inv) (by simp)).symm ≪≫
      MorphismProperty.Over.mapComp ⊤ (MorphismProperty.of_isIso finiteEtale e.hom)
        (MorphismProperty.of_isIso finiteEtale e.inv) (e.hom ≫ e.inv) rfl)
    ((MorphismProperty.Over.mapComp ⊤ (MorphismProperty.of_isIso finiteEtale e.inv)
        (MorphismProperty.of_isIso finiteEtale e.hom) (e.inv ≫ e.hom) rfl).symm ≪≫
      MorphismProperty.Over.mapId (P := finiteEtale) ⊤ Y (e.inv ≫ e.hom) (by simp))

/-- Base change of finite étale covers along an isomorphism is an equivalence: it is the right
adjoint of post-composition with that isomorphism, which is an equivalence. -/
private lemma isEquivalence_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_iso {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (e : X ≅ Y) :
    (finiteEtaleBaseChange e.hom).IsEquivalence :=
  Functor.isEquivalence_of_iso ((MorphismProperty.Over.mapPullbackAdj finiteEtale ⊤ e.hom
      (MorphismProperty.of_isIso finiteEtale e.hom) trivial).rightAdjointUniq
    (finiteEtaleOverMapEquivalence e).toAdjunction).symm

/-- Full faithfulness of base change of finite étale covers transports along an isomorphism of
arrows: base change along the two isomorphisms is an equivalence, and base change along a
composite is the composite of the base changes. -/
private lemma nonempty_fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_iso {X Y X' Y' : Scheme.{u}}
    {u : X ⟶ Y} {u' : X' ⟶ Y'} (a : X ≅ X') (b : Y ≅ Y') (h : u ≫ b.hom = a.hom ≫ u')
    (H : Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange u).FullyFaithful) :
    Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange u').FullyFaithful := by
  obtain ⟨hu⟩ := H
  have ha := isEquivalence_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_iso a
  have hb := isEquivalence_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_iso b
  have hbff : (finiteEtaleBaseChange b.hom).FullyFaithful :=
    .ofFullyFaithful (finiteEtaleBaseChange b.hom)
  have e : finiteEtaleBaseChange b.hom ⋙ finiteEtaleBaseChange u ≅
      finiteEtaleBaseChange u' ⋙ finiteEtaleBaseChange a.hom :=
    (MorphismProperty.Over.pullbackComp (P := finiteEtale) (Q := ⊤) u b.hom
        (u ≫ b.hom) rfl).symm ≪≫
      MorphismProperty.Over.pullbackCongr (P := finiteEtale) (Q := ⊤) h ≪≫
      MorphismProperty.Over.pullbackComp (P := finiteEtale) (Q := ⊤) a.hom u' (a.hom ≫ u') rfl
  exact ⟨Functor.FullyFaithful.ofCompFaithful (G := finiteEtaleBaseChange a.hom)
    ((hbff.comp hu).ofIso e)⟩

/-- Replacing the corner `c` of a cartesian square by an isomorphic object `Z` over the base:
`b' = b ≫ e.hom` is the new second leg and `e.hom ≫ fz = c`. -/
private lemma isPullback_of_iso_comp {C : Type*} [Category C] {P A X Z B : C} {a : P ⟶ A}
    {b : P ⟶ X} {b' : P ⟶ Z} {r : A ⟶ B} {c : X ⟶ B} {fz : Z ⟶ B} (e : X ≅ Z)
    (h : IsPullback a b r c) (hb : b ≫ e.hom = b') (he : e.hom ≫ fz = c) :
    IsPullback a b' r fz := by
  subst hb he
  exact h.of_iso (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) e (Iso.refl _) (by simp) (by simp) (by simp) (by simp)

/-- **The reduction of full faithfulness to the `f`-adically complete case.** In the local
Lefschetz situation assume `A` henselian, or more generally that `(A, fA)` is a henselian pair,
and let `P` be a property of local Lefschetz situations that holds for `S` and passes to the
completion. If restriction of finite étale covers `FÉt_T.U ⟶ FÉt_T.U₀` is fully faithful for
every `f`-adically complete situation `T` with property `P`, then `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` is fully
faithful.

This is Stacks 0BLI, applied to the local Lefschetz situation of the `𝔪`-adic completion: the
punctured spectra of `Â` and of `Â / fÂ` are the base changes to `Spec Â` of `U` and of `U₀`
that Stacks 0BLI speaks of. The passage of the side conditions to the completion is the
hypothesis `hPcompletion`, which for the two predicates the chapter needs is
`annihilated_completion` (Stacks 0ALZ) and `depthDim_completion` (Stacks 0EHW) above. -/
public theorem fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_isAdicCompleteCase
    (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u})
    (hS : HenselianLocalRing S.A ∨ HenselianPair S.A S.principalIdeal)
    (P : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u} → Prop) (hPS : P S)
    (hPcompletion : P S → P S.completion)
    (H : ∀ T : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}, IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {T.f}) T.A → P T →
      Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange T.U₀ToU).FullyFaithful) :
    Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange S.U₀ToU).FullyFaithful := by
  refine fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completion S hS ?_
  obtain ⟨cU, c₀, u₀, hcU, hU₀U, -⟩ := S.exists_isPullback_completion_U₀
  have hU₀U' : IsPullback u₀ (S.completion.U₀ToU ≫ hcU.isoPullback.hom) S.U₀ToU
      (pullback.fst S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap) :=
    isPullback_of_iso_comp hcU.isoPullback hU₀U rfl hcU.isoPullback_hom_fst
  exact nonempty_fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_iso hU₀U'.isoPullback hcU.isoPullback
    hU₀U'.isoPullback_hom_snd.symm
    (H S.completion S.isAdicComplete_completion (hPcompletion hPS))

/-- **Base change of the hypothesis that a cover of `U₀` comes from `X₀`.** Let `V ⟶ U` be a
morphism whose restriction `V ×_U U₀` is the base change of `Y₀ ⟶ X₀`, and let `cU : U' ⟶ U` and
`c₀ : X₀' ⟶ X₀` be morphisms along which `V'` is the base change of `V` and `U₀'` is the base
change of `U₀`, both over `U` and over `X₀`. Then the restriction `V' ×_{U'} U₀'` is the base
change of `Y₀ ×_{X₀} X₀' ⟶ X₀'`. -/
private lemma exists_isPullback_restriction_baseChange
    {V U U₀ X₀ V' U' U₀' X₀' Y₀ : Scheme.{u}}
    {pi : V ⟶ U} {j : U₀ ⟶ U} {i : U₀ ⟶ X₀} {f₀ : Y₀ ⟶ X₀} {cU : U' ⟶ U} {c₀ : X₀' ⟶ X₀}
    {j' : U₀' ⟶ U'} {i' : U₀' ⟶ X₀'} {pi' : V' ⟶ U'} {u₀ : U₀' ⟶ U₀} {w : V' ⟶ V}
    {g₀ : pullback pi j ⟶ Y₀}
    (hV' : IsPullback w pi' pi cU) (hU₀U : IsPullback u₀ j' j cU)
    (hU₀X₀ : IsPullback u₀ i' i c₀)
    (h₀ : IsPullback (pullback.snd pi j) g₀ i f₀) :
    ∃ e₀ : pullback pi' j' ⟶ pullback f₀ c₀,
      IsPullback (pullback.snd pi' j') e₀ i' (pullback.snd f₀ c₀) := by
  have hpaste : IsPullback (pullback.fst pi' j' ≫ w) (pullback.snd pi' j') pi (u₀ ≫ j) := by
    rw [hU₀U.w]
    exact (IsPullback.of_hasPullback pi' j').paste_horiz hV'
  have hV₀ := IsPullback.of_hasPullback pi j
  have hcond : (pullback.fst pi' j' ≫ w) ≫ pi = (pullback.snd pi' j' ≫ u₀) ≫ j := by
    simpa using hpaste.w
  have hstep1 : IsPullback (hV₀.lift (pullback.fst pi' j' ≫ w) (pullback.snd pi' j' ≫ u₀) hcond)
      (pullback.snd pi' j') (pullback.snd pi j) u₀ := by
    refine IsPullback.of_right (h₁₂ := pullback.fst pi j) ?_ (hV₀.lift_snd ..) hV₀
    rw [hV₀.lift_fst]
    exact hpaste
  have hstep2 : IsPullback (hV₀.lift (pullback.fst pi' j' ≫ w) (pullback.snd pi' j' ≫ u₀) hcond ≫
      g₀) (pullback.snd pi' j') f₀ (i' ≫ c₀) := by
    rw [← hU₀X₀.w]
    exact hstep1.paste_horiz h₀.flip
  have hZ₀ := IsPullback.of_hasPullback f₀ c₀
  have hcond₂ : (hV₀.lift (pullback.fst pi' j' ≫ w) (pullback.snd pi' j' ≫ u₀) hcond ≫ g₀) ≫ f₀
      = (pullback.snd pi' j' ≫ i') ≫ c₀ := by
    simpa using hstep2.w
  refine ⟨hZ₀.lift _ (pullback.snd pi' j' ≫ i') hcond₂, ?_⟩
  refine (IsPullback.of_right (h₁₂ := pullback.fst f₀ c₀) ?_ (hZ₀.lift_snd ..) hZ₀).flip
  rw [hZ₀.lift_fst]
  exact hstep2

/-- **The reduction of the existence of a finite étale extension to the `f`-adically complete
case.** In the local Lefschetz situation let `V` be finite étale over `U` with `V ×_U U₀` the base
change of a finite étale `Y₀ ⟶ X₀`, and let `P` be a property of local Lefschetz situations that
holds for `S` and passes to the completion. If in every `f`-adically complete situation with
property `P` every such cover extends to a finite étale scheme over `X`, then `V = Y ×_X U` for
some finite étale `Y ⟶ X`.

This is Stacks 0BLL, applied to the local Lefschetz situation of the `𝔪`-adic completion: that
tag says an extension over `Spec A` exists exactly when one exists over `Spec Â` for the base
change of `V`, and the punctured spectra of `Â` and of `Â / fÂ` are the base changes of `U` and
of `U₀` it speaks of. The hypothesis on `V ×_U U₀` travels to the completion by base change
along `Spec (Â / fÂ) ⟶ Spec (A / fA)`; the passage of the side conditions is the hypothesis
`hPcompletion`, which for the two predicates the chapter needs is `annihilated_completion`
(Stacks 0ALZ) and `depthDim_completion` (Stacks 0EHW) above. -/
public theorem exists_finiteEtale_extension_of_isAdicCompleteCase
    (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u})
    (P : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u} → Prop) (hPS : P S)
    (hPcompletion : P S → P S.completion)
    (H : ∀ T : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u}, IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {T.f}) T.A → P T →
      ∀ (W : Scheme.{u}) (p : W ⟶ T.U), IsFinite p → Etale p →
      ∀ (Z₀ : Scheme.{u}) (q₀ : Z₀ ⟶ T.X₀), IsFinite q₀ → Etale q₀ →
      ∀ e₀ : pullback p T.U₀ToU ⟶ Z₀,
        IsPullback (pullback.snd p T.U₀ToU) e₀ T.U₀Open.ι q₀ →
        ∃ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (r : Y ⟶ T.X) (g : W ⟶ Y),
          IsFinite r ∧ Etale r ∧ IsPullback p g T.UOpen.ι r)
    (V : Scheme.{u}) (pi : V ⟶ S.U) [IsFinite pi] [Etale pi]
    (Y₀ : Scheme.{u}) (f₀ : Y₀ ⟶ S.X₀) [IsFinite f₀] [Etale f₀]
    (g₀ : pullback pi S.U₀ToU ⟶ Y₀)
    (h₀ : IsPullback (pullback.snd pi S.U₀ToU) g₀ S.U₀Open.ι f₀) :
    ∃ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (p : Y ⟶ S.X) (g : V ⟶ Y),
      IsFinite p ∧ Etale p ∧ IsPullback pi g S.UOpen.ι p := by
  have key : ∃ (Yhat : Scheme.{u}) (rhat : Yhat ⟶ S.completion.X)
      (ghat : pullback pi (pullback.fst S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap) ⟶ Yhat),
      IsFinite rhat ∧ Etale rhat ∧
        IsPullback (pullback.snd pi (pullback.fst S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap)) ghat
          (pullback.snd S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap) rhat := by
    obtain ⟨cU, c₀, u₀, hcU, hU₀U, hU₀X₀⟩ := S.exists_isPullback_completion_U₀
    have hV' : IsPullback (pullback.fst pi (pullback.fst S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap))
        (pullback.snd pi (pullback.fst S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap) ≫ hcU.isoPullback.inv) pi cU :=
      isPullback_of_iso_comp hcU.isoPullback.symm
        (IsPullback.of_hasPullback pi (pullback.fst S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap)) rfl
        hcU.isoPullback_inv_fst
    have hfiniteEtale : finiteEtale (pullback.snd pi (pullback.fst S.UOpen.ι S.completionMap) ≫
        hcU.isoPullback.inv) :=
      finiteEtale.comp_mem _ _ ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩
        (MorphismProperty.of_isIso finiteEtale _)
    obtain ⟨e₀, he₀⟩ := exists_isPullback_restriction_baseChange hV' hU₀U hU₀X₀ h₀
    obtain ⟨Y, r, g, hrfinite, hretale, hr⟩ :=
      H S.completion S.isAdicComplete_completion (hPcompletion hPS) _ _ hfiniteEtale.1
        hfiniteEtale.2 (pullback f₀ c₀) (pullback.snd f₀ c₀) inferInstance inferInstance e₀ he₀
    exact ⟨Y, r, g, hrfinite, hretale,
      (isPullback_of_iso_comp hcU.isoPullback hr.flip (by simp)
        hcU.isoPullback_hom_snd).flip⟩
  exact (exists_finiteEtale_extension_iff_completion S.A V pi).mpr key

end LocalLefschetzSituation

end AlgebraicGeometry

